  winning record which they've done every  year since 2003 or non-losing records  since 2003 gives them a chance to do  that go back to the playoffs but i just  don't see this as a as a team in  contention mike with or without ben  roethlisberger  i still think it's a mistake and i still  think both sides are going to live to  regret this in november or december and  they're going to say we just shouldn't  have done it that's my prediction i  could end up on freezing cold takes with  that quote at some point down the road i  just think it makes more sense if you  don't reasonably believe you're going to  win the super bowl it makes more sense  to just move on now and one of the  things sims and i discussed today we are  smack dab in that period of the  offseason where confidence runs a muck  in the various team facilities you're  far enough removed from what happened  last season and you're deep enough into  your thoughts of well if we just do this  if we just do this if we just do that  we're going to win the super bowl i  think it's easy to get caught up in the  sense of delusion that you can make the  climb all the way up to the top of the  stack and  i just don't think that that's realistic  and i really do think both sides would  be better off moving on  i think both sides are concerned about  how the fan base will react this is  going to be an awkward parting of the  ways  and maybe the only  non-awkward way to do it or the least  awkward way to do it is to let everyone  know  that this  is it a year from now there may be some  fans that say let's do it again see  that's the problem shireen if they get  to the afc championship this year  won't there be  a sense a desire  an argument to be made that they should  run it back one more time and keep doing  that until you have that year where you  do regret it anything other than winning  the super bowl is going to create that  same sense of well let's give it one  more shot let's give it one more shot  let's give 