e not doing any you know mr miyagi  thing to try to make the knees better if  he just has arthritis well guess what if  that's the case it ain't getting any  better it's not going to be better when  everyone is a year older so yeah i think  they're either what what  whatever they think they're going to be  and i think continuing this relationship  is kind of a subtle message that they  think they can be damn good here it is  in the statement i told ben that we  would like to have him back to help us  win  a championship that's the bar not afc  north championship a championship so  regret means they're going to get to a  point  thanksgiving maybe sooner maybe later  where they say crap we ain't going to  win a championship we'd have been better  off starting down the path of seeing  what we have in mason rudolph seeing  what we have in dwayne haskins drafting  someone trading up doing something to  begin this post ben roethlisberger  existence because now what's going to  happen is they're not going to win a  championship they're going to have to do  it next year  but here's the thing mike if say he  exits week two like he did two years ago  hey we're expecting full stadiums at  that point the stadium is full which i  understand steelers fans always come out  maybe it's full if they start mason  rudolph maybe it's full if they start  dwayne haskins who knows maybe it's for  whoever they start at quarterback but i  do know it will be full if ben  roethlisberger is there week one whether  he exits week two or week ten or week  whatever it is he the stadium is going  to be full and those steelers fans are  going to be excited that ben  roethlisberger has come back for one  more year they're going to sell a lot of  jerseys they're going to do all those  things and they're going to make some  money off of this but  i i get it and and i understand you know  maybe it is time to look at dwayne  haskins or look at mason rudolph and  start that hard reset button on a team  that's not going to be able to go out  and get a big name quarterback to help  this franchise it's probably going to  lose bud dupree and some of those other  free agents that they have but i know  they're looking at hey we were 11-0 to  start the season and as you said mike  you get far enough away from that season  you forget how december ended you forget  those five interceptions that been  through in december and you say hey we  can get back to that point where we were  11-0 with ben  you've touched on what i am now going to  refer to as the nfl's version of the big  lie and that is that when they say the  goal is to win a championship the truth  is the goal is to make wait for it  as much money as they possibly can and  in order to make as much money as they  possibly can they have to say not  we're going to try to bring ben back and  make as much money as we possibly can  they have to say we're going to try to  win a championship  if you truly determine whether or not  you're successful based on winning a  championship you are pissed off every  year sorry london the patriots fail more  than two-thirds of the time one of the  best teams we've ever seen still a  failure more than two-thirds of the time  because they've only won six  championships in the last 20 years so  this very well may be this may vary  let's just fill the stadium let's make  everybody happy let's not upset the  apple cart this is our first year  post pandemic we got a lot of salty fans  who resent the fact that they weren't  able to come last year let's just give  them one more year of ben roethlisberger  let's give them what they want they get  to see ben for one more year wouldn't it  be a shame if in his last year there  were no fans that got to see him so  let's let them see ben for one more year  and then we'll deal with it next year  that may be the truth  but they ain't going to put that in the  statement sharing  no absolutely they're not mike and  frankly the quarterback market maybe 